### Phase 18: Performance Optimization Testing

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@accessToken = your_access_token_here

### ============================================
### 1. Health Check & Performance Metrics
### ============================================

### Test 1.1: Enhanced Health Check with Cache Stats
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

# Expected response includes:
# - memory usage
# - cache stats (connected, keys, memory, hit rate)
# - performance metrics (avgDuration, slowRequests, errorRequests)

###

### ============================================
### 2. Redis Connection Test
### ============================================

### Test 2.1: Verify Redis is Running
# Run in terminal: docker ps | grep redis
# Expected: agrimarket-redis container running

### Test 2.2: Ping Redis
# Run in terminal: docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli ping
# Expected: PONG

### Test 2.3: Check Redis Memory
# Run in terminal: docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli INFO memory

###

### ============================================
### 3. Caching Tests - Products
### ============================================

### Test 3.1: First Request (Cache Miss)
# @name productList1
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Note response time (should be slower - database query)

###

### Test 3.2: Second Request (Cache Hit)
# @name productList2
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Note response time (should be ~90% faster - from cache)
# Expected: < 50ms response time

###

### Test 3.3: Product Detail (Cache Miss)
# @name productDetail1
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/clx123456789
Accept: application/json

###

### Test 3.4: Product Detail (Cache Hit)
# @name productDetail2
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/clx123456789
Accept: application/json

# Expected: Much faster than first request

###

### Test 3.5: Cache Invalidation - Update Product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/clx123456789
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Product Name",
  "description": "This should invalidate product caches"
}

# This should clear all product caches

###

### Test 3.6: Verify Cache Cleared - Product List
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Should be slower (cache miss after invalidation)

###

### ============================================
### 4. Caching Tests - Search
### ============================================

### Test 4.1: Search Query (Cache Miss)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=tomato&page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Note response time

###

### Test 4.2: Same Search Query (Cache Hit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=tomato&page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Expected: ~95% faster than first request

###

### Test 4.3: Autocomplete (Cache Miss)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?q=tom
Accept: application/json

###

### Test 4.4: Autocomplete (Cache Hit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?q=tom
Accept: application/json

# Expected: Very fast (<30ms)

###

### Test 4.5: Popular Searches (Cached 15 minutes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/popular
Accept: application/json

# Expected: Fast response, 15-minute cache

###

### ============================================
### 5. Caching Tests - Categories
### ============================================

### Test 5.1: Get All Categories (Cache Miss)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories
Accept: application/json

# Categories cached for 1 hour (rarely change)

###

### Test 5.2: Get All Categories (Cache Hit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories
Accept: application/json

# Expected: Very fast (<20ms)

###

### Test 5.3: Get Category by Slug (Cache Miss)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/vegetables
Accept: application/json

###

### Test 5.4: Get Category by Slug (Cache Hit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/vegetables
Accept: application/json

# Expected: Very fast

