### ============================================
### 9. Performance Measurement
### ============================================

### Test 9.1: Response Time Comparison Script
# Run multiple requests and compare:
# 1. First request (cache miss): ~200-800ms
# 2. Second request (cache hit): ~20-50ms
# 3. Improvement: 90-97%

###

### Test 9.2: Load Test with Artillery
# Create artillery-test.yml and run:
# artillery run artillery-test.yml

###

### Test 9.3: Measure Cache Hit Rate
# After running requests, check health endpoint
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

# Check: cache.hitRate
# Target: > 70%

###

### ============================================
### 10. Cache Management
### ============================================

### Test 10.1: Check Cache Keys
# Run in terminal:
# docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli KEYS "agrimarket:*"

###

### Test 10.2: Check Cache Key TTL
# Run in terminal:
# docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli TTL "agrimarket:response:/api/v1/products"

###

### Test 10.3: Manual Cache Clear (if needed)
# Run in terminal:
# docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli FLUSHDB

###

### Test 10.4: Monitor Cache in Real-Time
# Run in terminal:
# docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli MONITOR

###

### ============================================
### 11. Performance Regression Tests
### ============================================

### Test 11.1: Slow Request Detection
# Make 20 concurrent requests to trigger slow request detection
# Check logs for "Slow request detected" messages

###

### Test 11.2: Performance Metrics Endpoint
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

# Check performance.avgDuration
# Target: < 100ms average

###

### ============================================
### 12. Cache Invalidation Patterns
### ============================================

### Test 12.1: Product Update Invalidates Product Caches
# 1. GET /products (cached)
# 2. PUT /products/:id (invalidates)
# 3. GET /products (cache miss - should refetch)

###

### Test 12.2: Category Update Invalidates Category Caches
# 1. GET /categories (cached)
# 2. PUT /categories/:id (invalidates)
# 3. GET /categories (cache miss)

###

### Test 12.3: User Actions Invalidate User Caches
# 1. GET /cart (cached per user)
# 2. POST /cart/items (invalidates user cache)
# 3. GET /cart (cache miss for that user)

###

### ============================================
### 13. Redis Persistence Test
### ============================================

### Test 13.1: Restart Redis Container
# Run in terminal:
# docker restart agrimarket-redis
# Wait 5 seconds

###

### Test 13.2: Check Data Persisted
# Make a cached request - should be cache miss (Redis restarted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

###

### Test 13.3: Rebuild Cache
# Make the same request again
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

# Should now be cached

###

### ============================================
### 14. Memory Usage Tests
### ============================================

### Test 14.1: Check Redis Memory Usage
# Run in terminal:
# docker exec -it agrimarket-redis redis-cli INFO memory | grep used_memory_human

# Expected: < 256MB (configured max)

###

### Test 14.2: Check Application Memory
GET http://localhost:5000/health
Accept: application/json

# Check: memory.used
# Expected: < 512MB

###

### ============================================
### 15. Cache Warming (Optional)
### ============================================

### Test 15.1: Warm Up Product Cache
# Pre-populate cache with most accessed endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10&category=vegetables
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/recommendations/trending
GET {{baseUrl}}/recommendations/best-sellers

###

### ============================================
### Performance Testing Checklist
### ============================================

# [ ] Redis container is running
# [ ] Application connects to Redis successfully
# [ ] Cache hits show faster response times (>90% improvement)
# [ ] Cache invalidation works correctly
# [ ] User-specific caching isolates user data
# [ ] Health endpoint shows cache statistics
# [ ] Cache hit rate > 70%
# [ ] Average response time < 100ms (cached)
# [ ] No memory leaks after extended use
# [ ] Redis persistence works (survives restarts)

###
